orner of the town walls and permitted access to the town from the Platform and Town Quay. It is now an arts and heritage venue, and has previously served as the town gaol and housed the Museum of Archaeology.","wpu":"God's House Tower","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2a/Gods_house_tower_2021.JPG/960px-Gods_house_tower_2021.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Tudor House Museum","g":"sights","k":"museum","la":50.899498,"lo":-1.406141,"d":289,"w":"https://www.tudorhouseandgarden.com/","wp":"en:Tudor House and Garden","ds":"Tudor House and Garden is a historic building, museum, tourist attraction, and Grade I listed building in Southampton, England. Established as Southampton's first museum in 1912, the house was closed for nine years between 2002 and 2011 during an extensive renovation. The house is located in Bugle Street, opposite St.","wpu":"Tudor House and Garden","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/Tudor_House%2C_Southampton.jpg/960px-Tudor_House%2C_Southampton.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"King John's Palace","g":"sights","k":"ruins","la":50.899504,"lo":-1.406662,"d":301},{"n":"Church of Holyrood","g":"sights","k":"ruins","la":50.899697,"lo":-1.40333,"d":321,"wp":"en:Holyrood Church","ds":"Holyrood Church (or Holy Rood Church) was one of the original five churches serving the old walled town of Southampton, England. Built in 1320, the church was destroyed by enemy bombing during the blitz in November 1940. In 1957 the shell of the church was dedicated as a memorial to the sailors of the Merchant Navy.","wpu":"Holyrood Church","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/Chancel_of_Holyrood_Church%2C_Southampton.jpg/960px-Chancel_of_Holyrood_Church%2C_Southampton.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Undercroft","g":"sights","k":"attraction","la":50.900106,"lo":-1.405748,"d":349},{"n":"Leonardo Royal Hotel","g":"sights","k":"hotel","la":50.899713,"lo":-1.407693,"d":355,"wifi":1},{"n":"Southampton Castle Garderobe Tower","g":"sights","k":"ruins","la":50.900741,"lo":-1.406403,"d":427},{"n":"Southampton Castle","g":"sights","k":"ruins","la":50.900826,"lo":-1.406233,"d":434,"ds":"Southampton Castle was located in the town of Southampton in Hampshire, England. Constructed after the Norman conquest of England, it was located in the north-west corner of the town overlooking the River Test, initially as a wooden motte and bailey design.","wpu":"Southampton Castle","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/c/cd/Map_of_Southampton_Castle.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"},{"n":"Travelodge","g":"sights","k":"hotel","la":50.900899,"lo":-1.404554,"d":434,"w":"https://www.travelodge.co.uk/hotels/589/Southampton-Central-hotel","wifi":1},{"n":"Castle Gate","g":"sights","k":"attraction","la":50.901373,"lo":-1.404907,"d":486},{"n":"Catchcold Tower","g":"sights","k":"monument","la":50.902275,"lo":-1.406035,"d":591},{"n":"Premier Inn - West Quay","g":"sights","k":"hotel","la":50.901985,"lo":-1.408215,"d":598,"w":"https://www.premierinn.com/gb/en/hotels/england/hampshire/southampton/southampton-city-centre-west-quay.html","wifi":1},{"n":"Arundel Tower","g":"sights","k":"monument","la":50.902664,"lo":-1.406041,"d":633},{"n":"William Chamberlayne Gas Column 1822","g":"sights","k":"monument","la":50.903191,"lo":-1.401854,"d":722},{"n":"Charles Melly Memorial Fountain 1859","g":"sights","k":"monument","la":50.903886,"lo":-1.401925,"d":795},{"n":"Solent Sky","g":"sights","k":"museum","la":50.897916,"lo":-1.39308,"d":842,"h":"Mo-Sa 10:00-17:00; Su 12:00-17:00","w":"https://www.solentsky.org/","ph":"+44 2380 635 830","wp":"en:Solent Sky","ds":"Solent Sky (previously known as the Southampton Hall of Aviation) is an aviation museum in Southampton, England. The museum depicts the history of aviation in Southampton, the Solent area and Hampshire. There is a focus on Supermarine, the aircraft company based in Woolston, Southampton, and its most famous products, the Supermarine S.6 seaplane and the Supermarine Spitfire, designed by a team led R. J. Mitchell.","wpu":"Solent Sky","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/90/Solent_Sky_general_view.JPG/960px-Solent_Sky_general_view.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Calshot Spit Lightship","g":"sights","k":"attraction","la":50.897961,"lo":-1.392653,"d":872,"wp":"en:LV 78 Calshot Spit","ds":"LV 78 Calshot Spit is a former Trinity House lightvessel that was anchored off Calshot Spit and is now a museum ship in Southampton. LV 78 was built in 1914 by John I. Thornycroft & Company shipyard in Southampton and decommissioned in 1987. She was stationed at the entrance to the Port of Southampton to act as a floating lighthouse to guide ships and flying boats entering Southampton Water.","wpu":"LV 78 Calshot Spit","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/a6/Calshot_Spit_lightvessel.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"},{"n":"Ibis Budget","g":"sights","k":"hotel","la":50.904991,"lo":-1.41414,"d":1095,"wifi":1},{"n":"John Hansard Gallery","g":"sights","k":"gallery","la":50.907927,"lo":-1.404158,"d":1216,"h":"Tu-Sa 11:00-17:00","w":"https://jhg.art","wp":"en:John Hansard Gallery","ds":"The John Hansard Gallery is a contemporary visual art gallery and part of the University of Southampton.","wpu":"John Hansard Gallery","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/2/20/John_Hansard_Gallery.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"},{"n":"Premier Inn","g":"sights","k":"hotel","la":50.907248,"lo":-1.398526,"d":1226,"w":"https://www.premierinn.com/gb/en/hotels/england/hampshire/southampton/southampton-city-centre.html","wifi":1},{"n":"SeaCity Museum","g":"si