":"sights","k":"landmark","la":50.90287,"lo":-1.39506,"d":954,"ds":"Saint Mary's Church, is the civic church for the city of Southampton, Hampshire, England. Originally founded in circa 634, St Mary's has been the mother church of Southampton since its inception.","wpu":"St Mary's Church, Southampton","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/St_Mary%27s_Southampton.jpg/960px-St_Mary%27s_Southampton.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Franciscan Friary, Southampton","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":50.907086,"lo":-1.400436,"d":1166,"ds":"The Franciscan Friary of Southampton was founded c. 1233. It occupied a south-eastern area of the city, within the walls and adjacent to God's House Tower.","wpu":"Franciscan Friary, Southampton","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/4/4e/Southampton_Friary.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"},{"n":"Blechynden Terrace Park","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":50.90771,"lo":-1.41167,"d":1279,"ds":"Blechynden Terrace Park or Blechynden Gardens is a park in Southampton, Hampshire, England. It lies within the remains of the Emperia Building, which was destroyed by German bombing during World War II. As part of a 2018 beautification scheme. a 4.9m corten steel arch was placed over the main path through the park.","wpu":"Blechynden Terrace Park","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/Blechynden_Terrace_Park_twilight.JPG/960px-Blechynden_Terrace_Park_twilight.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Mayflower Theatre","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":50.90855,"lo":-1.41024,"d":1335,"ds":"Mayflower Theatre (formerly the Gaumont Theatre and originally the Empire Theatre) is a Grade II listed theatre in the city centre of Southampton, England. With a capacity of 2,300, it features West End theatre shows when they tour the United Kingdom. In addition to this, one-off comedy shows and music events often take place at the theatre too.","wpu":"Mayflower Theatre","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/83/Mayflower_Theatre%2C_Commercial_Road%2C_Southampton_%28NHLE_Code_1092039%29_%28July_2021%29_%282%29.jpg/960px-Mayflower_Theatre%2C_Commercial_Road%2C_Southampton_%28NHLE_Code_1092039%29_%28July_2021%29_%282%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Itchen Bridge","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":50.8988,"lo":-1.3847,"d":1437,"ds":"The Itchen Bridge is a bridge over the River Itchen in Southampton, Hampshire. It is a high-level hollow box girder bridge. It is located about a mile from the river mouth.","wpu":"Itchen Bridge","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/6/6d/Itchen_Bridge_in_2007_HDR.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"},{"n":"Titanic Engineers' Memorial","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":50.91018,"lo":-1.40469,"d":1465,"ds":"The Titanic Engineers' Memorial is a memorial in East (Andrews) Park, Southampton, United Kingdom, to the engineers who died in the Titanic disaster on 15 April 1912. The bronze and granite memorial was originally unveiled by Sir Archibald Denny, president of the Institute of Marine Engineers on 22 April 1914. The event was attended by an estimated 100,000 Southampton residents.","wpu":"Titanic Engineers' Memorial","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Titanic_Engineers_Memorial_2017.JPG/960px-Titanic_Engineers_Memorial_2017.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"River Itchen, Hampshire","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":50.9052,"lo":-1.38565,"d":1634,"ds":"The River Itchen in Hampshire, England, rises to the south of New Alresford and flows 26 miles (42 km) to meet Southampton Water below the Itchen Bridge. The Itchen Navigation was constructed in the late 17th and early 18th centuries to enable barges to reach Winchester from Southampton Docks, but ceased to operate in the mid-19th century and is largely abandoned today.","wpu":"River Itchen, Hampshire","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3a/River_Itchen_Ovington.jpg/960px-River_Itchen_Ovington.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"}],"about":{"ds":"Rockstone Place Park or Little Mongers Park is a formal park in Southampton, United Kingdom. The park is next to the Southampton and New Forest Magistrates court building. The park was originally constructed in the 19th century as a pleasure garden for the residents of a nearby housing development.","wpu":"Rockstone Place Park","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/db/Rockstone_Place_Park.JPG/960px-Rockstone_Place_Park.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},"wk":"2026-10-18"}